  "short_description": "Non-canonical FirstPersonEmbodiment research layered on accepted CH9.6, with S4 first-person two-hand grip accepted and S5 evaluating third-person secondary-hand support through native TwoBoneIK3D or a collision-free fallback procedural arm.",
  "purpose": "Evaluate first-person articulated one/two-hand held-item presentation, third-person held-item visibility and secondary-hand support, catalogued item silhouettes, grip profiles, clothing-visible viewmodels and low-latency item selection without reopening frozen CH9.6 and without weakening authority over concrete item actions.",
  "expected_outcome": "The selected canonical replica item resolves through presentation-only visual/grip catalogs. One-hand items occupy only the primary right hand. Two-hand profiles reserve the left articulated first-person hand and, in third person, drive the world-avatar left arm toward the same secondary grip target using native Skeleton3D TwoBoneIK3D where available or a presentation-only fallback arm solver when the graphical lab is using the fallback humanoid. Empty/one-hand selection restores both left-hand presentations immediately. Concrete item mutations remain server-authoritative and hotbar selection remains transient/local.",
  "current_stage": "FPE-R2 S5 Fix2 — replica mount-base classification precedence",
  "stage_status": "RESEARCH_R2_S5_FIX2_OPERATOR_RERUN_PENDING",
  "progress_note": "R2/S1 remains accepted with clean focused and graphical evidence. R2/S2 and R2/S3 were revalidated by the clean full S4 focused suite on 8754891d; S3 also has graphical evidence with articulated fingers visibly wrapping the selected item. R2/S4 is accepted for research progression with clean focused evidence and operator-confirmed zero self-push sandbox physics. S5 Fix1 removed an inherited VisualFactoryType compile collision. The operator then ran a clean full suite on 5bafc479, including S5 secondary-hand support 33 assertions, S5 two-hand third-person presenter 20, collision isolation 30, performance 10 and graphical scene-load 22. The following graphical run exposed a coverage gap: switching slot 1 to slot 2 changed item identity/color but the right hand remained beacon_pinch, S4 remained FREE and S5 remained FREE. Root cause is now confirmed: the accepted M7 replica adapter maps canonical item/mount-base to replica definition beacon_mount_base. Both ItemViewmodelCatalog and HeldItemGripProfileCatalog matched the generic beacon token before the more specific mountbase token. The old tests used item/mount-base and therefore missed the actual replica identity collision. Fix2 gives mount-base family precedence in both catalogs. beacon_mount_base now resolves BOX/mount_base plus mount_base_two_hand instead of CYLINDER/beacon plus beacon_vertical. Regression coverage now uses the actual replica definition and accepted tags assembly_root/placeable/mount_socket. Accepted CH9.6 remains unchanged.",
  "last_accepted_checkpoint": "FPE-R2 S4 RESEARCH ACCEPTED: clean full focused suite on 8754891dad2300eeb9a2e60e9a8a6e3482dcaee1 plus operator-confirmed zero self-push sandbox physics; accepted CH9.6 base e547ba52a440e72cc02c6bbe449edaf160bae7ab remains frozen",
  "next_stage": "Operator updates the detached FPE worktree and reruns RUN_FPE_RESEARCH_TESTS.ps1. The S2 catalog gate now explicitly validates replica definition beacon_mount_base and should report 27 assertions; S4 two-hand grip contract now also uses beacon_mount_base. Then run PLAY_FPE_RESEARCH.ps1. In first person slot 1 must report R:beacon_pinch and S4 FREE; slot 2 must switch the right pose away from beacon_pinch, report profile mount_base_two_hand and S4 ACTIVE with left support_cradle. In third person slot 2 must report S5 world left ACTIVE with FALLBACK_PROCEDURAL_ARM on the current fallback avatar. Slot 1/empty must release secondary support. Switching while moving must remain zero-stall.",
